#{[{:activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186231895} :activity/id #uuid "9064539b-24fc-5d46-a38d-08655e37a357" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048846 :topic/id #uuid "c59fe2ed-0027-529f-b6e0-3d5e566657df" :topic/math-academy-id 6769} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186231895 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186232014 :tutorial/content "So far, we have considered the area of a *right triangle*.\nBut what is the area of a *general* triangle, one that is not necessarily a right triangle?\n\nIt turns out that the same idea still works.\n\n> A formula for the area of a triangle is\n> $\\textrm{Area} = \\dfrac{1}{2} \\cdot b \\cdot h$,\n> where $b$ is the base and $h$ is the corresponding height.\n\nThis formula works for *any* triangle.\n\nLet's use this formula to find the area of the triangle below.\n\n![](images/e7/e7c8eaf780eaa0559e8ac4dc2557a423b805705bfd3a081635f5284502896168.png)\n\nIn our triangle,\n\n$$\n\\textrm{base} = 7 \\: \\text{ft}, \\qquad \\textrm{height} = 3 \\: \\text{ft}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of the triangle is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nArea &= \\frac{1}{2} \\cdot 7 \\cdot 3 \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{2} \\cdot 21 \\\\\n&= 10.5ft^{2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAt the end of this lesson, we'll show how to prove the formula for the area of a triangle.\n\nLet’s see more examples." :tutorial/id #uuid "35bf275f-a5b4-5e22-8a11-a01a18b1bd80" :tutorial/math-academy-id 14876 :tutorial/title "Introduction"} :step/id #uuid "20b0a099-6ca9-5ba0-b3a5-942ce21c5dd3" :step/math-academy-id 632546 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186231896}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186231896 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186231464 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186231397 :question/id #uuid "5821763d-6de9-557f-9688-a690b09082ce" :question/math-academy-id "e-2634"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b4c3c332-b81e-5dc9-a031-2d5635bd2e24" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049249}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186231764} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186231765} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186515614}] :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Area of a Triangle Given the Base and Height as Whole Numbers"} :step/id #uuid "88098e77-a8d8-51f6-9125-96ff2b4eb4d0" :step/math-academy-id 632547 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186231897}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186231897 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186231465 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186231398 :question/id #uuid "6a25b580-e4dc-51c4-b807-87810e4a5deb" :question/math-academy-id "e-2636"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8ed43817-53c7-5896-9848-73cb2209c39d" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186231767} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186231768} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186515615}] :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Area of a Triangle: Word Problem"} :step/id #uuid "c34b726a-fd07-5d01-a3ce-1006d2aca94b" :step/math-academy-id 632550 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186231898}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186231898 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186231466 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186231399 :question/id #uuid "72173b80-8f7e-5e3f-8185-974455c90509" :question/math-academy-id "e-2637"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "68d79c4f-277f-5010-a99b-3e1d99b4d433" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048523}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186231763} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186231769}] :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Base of a Triangle Given the Height and Area"} :step/id #uuid "fe5c0cda-3d44-5857-87a2-559959c7d8a2" :step/math-academy-id 632553 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186231899}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186231899 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186232013 :tutorial/content "We know that the area formula for a triangle is\n\n$$\n\\mathcal{A} = \\dfrac{1}{2} \\cdot b \\cdot h\n$$\n\nwhere $b$ is a base and $h$ is the corresponding height.\n\nBut where does this formula come from?\n\nTo understand this, consider the triangle below, with base $b$ and height $h$.\n\n![](images/b0/b0fa27c8446b799668c5493fa2049eb10550134724dc5e54aab8628a33857f0e.png)\n\nLet's draw a rectangle around it, as follows:\n\n![](images/aa/aa8ae2b0c13e0710a8316c920a4d62e0fe822095311d11f4ca3381f022585725.png)\n\nWe have two pairs of right triangles with equal areas (each pair is indicated with arrows).\n\nThe area of the enclosing rectangle is $b \\cdot h$. Since the triangle occupies exactly half of this area, we have\n\n$$\n\\mathcal{A} = \\dfrac{1}{2} \\cdot b \\cdot h\n$$" :tutorial/id #uuid "8b463fce-69c3-5e1f-b5c1-15b44aaf6f50" :tutorial/math-academy-id 14875 :tutorial/title "Proof of the Formula For the Area of a Triangle"} :step/id #uuid "d3617bdf-e6ac-5e17-865e-8d3291845e2e" :step/math-academy-id 632556}] :activity/title "Areas of Triangles" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :activity.type/lesson} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186231547}] [{:activity/course {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186046647} :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186515648} :activity/id #uuid "171482d0-9733-5990-af68-52e897a70b2e" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048846 :topic/id #uuid "c59fe2ed-0027-529f-b6e0-3d5e566657df" :topic/math-academy-id 6769} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186515648 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186515614 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5fa01b50-fa86-5d42-9d9e-f20c208a1076" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "72\\,{\\text{in}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515079} {:answer/id #uuid "8ec4b3e2-e623-5ec4-96cf-21891cfd3080" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "126\\,{\\text{in}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515173} {:answer/id #uuid "99fdabb5-1a73-59b9-810d-855b3e1bb6d4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "63\\,{\\text{in}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515198} {:answer/id #uuid "c88701b7-a7fa-56ab-8c32-e6f1ba45d2a8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "144\\,{\\text{in}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515298} {:answer/id #uuid "f083bac5-dd38-5485-a153-68c65a64f5f0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "98\\,{\\text{in}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515377}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186515079} :answer-field/id #uuid "765d86ee-70ad-5e5c-a6c0-9172acef54c7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515452}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "e9fe6faf-8364-54c6-b5c6-ec03e2fb9a2a" :question/math-academy-id "q-60624" :question/problem "![](images/43/435f50f68f1d5d206a935ec9b00dcd53e7a68647875e21f36d70379e3915a4c5.png)\n\nFind the area of the triangle." :question/worked-solution "First, we find the height and base of the triangle:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{base} & =12 \\\\ \\text{height} & =12\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe area of the triangle can be found by the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}=\\frac{1}{2}\\times \\text{base}\\times \\text{height}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the values of the base and height, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Area} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\times 12\\times 12 \\\\  & =6\\times 12 \\\\  & =72.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's find the units. Since base and height are measured in inches, the area is measured in square inches. Hence,\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}=72\\,{\\text{in}}^{2}.\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "417d8d63-6e21-5e67-9747-6630e9445dd3" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186515686}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186515667 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186515615 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "04136959-5e41-5216-9279-1057512c0bff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "12\\,{\\text{ft}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186514880} {:answer/id #uuid "43cbd2ae-0ecf-5595-a730-c4685cb767c2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "22.5\\,{\\text{ft}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515017} {:answer/id #uuid "5034e216-50cc-5f90-9470-0f87b0b6f66d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "35\\,{\\text{ft}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515049} {:answer/id #uuid "68c29f71-725a-5607-b616-c53b49800b36" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "24\\,{\\text{ft}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515091} {:answer/id #uuid "c16fb5a3-adb1-598c-a1b6-a5eb383b33bb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "17.5\\,{\\text{ft}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515282}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186515282} :answer-field/id #uuid "5a740dc6-0953-53ea-b78c-39bc996dc617" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515440}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "ecf8daef-9b17-549e-9c51-518ec81d55ec" :question/math-academy-id "q-93149" :question/problem "Claire has sectioned off a triangular area of her garden whose base is $7$ feet and height is $5$ feet to plant some flowers. What is the area of the flowerbed?" :question/worked-solution "Let's sketch the flowerbed based on the description.\n\n![](images/b4/b409d299208280d3be7e33be8e74c3d894fa9f3ad7e5605e4b551b6b0434302a.png)\n\nThe height and base of the triangle are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{base} & =7, \\\\ \\text{height} & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe area of the triangle can be found by the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}=\\frac{1}{2}\\times \\text{base}\\times \\text{height}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the values of the base and height, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Area} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\times 7\\times 5 \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\times 35 \\\\  & =17.5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's find the units. Since base and height are measured in feet, the area is measured in square feet. Hence,\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}=17.5\\,{\\text{ft}}^{2}.\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "8acdd2d7-5504-5f14-bf0e-df9ca76ee416"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186515686 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186231768 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2e40f59c-5c43-5ce3-9fec-419a42be11b6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "7.5\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186514975} {:answer/id #uuid "6ad3516e-b294-5e7c-a474-d9e0c1c6b4cf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "12.5\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515093} {:answer/id #uuid "a371e2e3-b68a-5d88-b845-9048a4af13b4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "15\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515220} {:answer/id #uuid "f399ef28-c29c-5938-afa7-1520d202501d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "9.5\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515384} {:answer/id #uuid "f445b4ca-4a23-598d-8e00-2f709f5f07d9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "25\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515385}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186514975} :answer-field/id #uuid "4dd91ab1-bff9-5024-b786-11dfd18c92a5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186231170}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "ab0bd4df-9796-5f7d-9c14-c1ed510ea0c1" :question/math-academy-id "q-60640" :question/problem "Nicole bakes triangular cakes with a base of $5$ cm and a height of $3$ cm. What is the area of one cake?" :question/worked-solution "Let's sketch our cake based on the description.\n\n![](images/20/205df21c66b54b84f9b0608baebf49277720738e1fac14219a7631848ea5c19a.png)\n\nThe height and base of the triangle are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{base} & =5, \\\\ \\text{height} & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe area of the triangle can be found by the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}=\\frac{1}{2}\\times \\text{base}\\times \\text{height}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the values of the base and height, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Area} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\times 5\\times 3 \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\times 15 \\\\  & =7.5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's find the units. Since base and height are measured in centimeters, the area is measured in square centimeters. Hence,\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}=7.5\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}.\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "b8dfeb6a-a542-5081-9a28-e226e6553d95" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186515667}}] :activity/title "Areas of Triangles" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186514853}]}
